TEXT -96 -256 Left 2 ;Problem 1.1 - duality of DC circuits.  Top: the circuit with impedances Z = R.  Bottom: its dual, with admittances Y = 1/R.
TEXT -96 -224 Left 2 ;LTspice only has resistors, so the dual's conductances are typed in as resistor values (G1 = 1/R1 = 10m ...): same numbers, units swap V <-> A.
TEXT 640 -32 Left 2 ;v3 = v0 Z2 Z3 / (Z1 (Z2+Z3) + Z2 Z3) = 8 V
TEXT 640 0 Left 2 ;i1 = I(R1) = 20 mA,  v1 = 2 V,  i2 = 4 mA,  i3 = 16 mA
TEXT 640 368 Left 2 ;dual: every current above is a voltage here and vice versa
TEXT 640 400 Left 2 ;V(d_i1) = 20 mV (= i1),  I(R_G2) = 8 A (= v3),  I(R_G1) = 2 A (= v1),  V(d_i3) = 16 mV (= i3)
TEXT -96 640 Left 2 !.op
TEXT -96 688 Left 2 ;Run, then hover the wires / resistors (or View > SPICE Error Log) to read the operating point.
